  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="aad09769-9fdc-553b-91c4-4c21aadb73a1" activityNameId="3578e062-22ed-5b65-b9e4-f501e9febd70" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, aluminium, 0% water, to municipal incineration</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, aluminium, 0% water, to municipal incineration
This dataset represents the activity of waste disposal of scrap aluminium in a municipal solid waste incinerator (MSWI) Recommended use of this dataset: For disposal of bulky, non-dust aluminium, which goes to disposal as part of a larger item or in small amounts only. Pure, isolated aluminium fractions will not be disposed in incinerators or landfills, but rather go to recycling. Waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O n.a.; O n.a.; H n.a.; C n.a.; S n.a.; N n.a.; P n.a.; B n.a.; Cl 4825; Br n.a.; F n.a.; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As n.a.; Ba n.a.; Cd 3; Co n.a.; Cr n.a.; Cu 8.5; Hg n.a.; Mn n.a.; Mo n.a.; Ni n.a.; Pb 25.5; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V n.a.; Zn 29; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti n.a.; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si n.a.; Fe n.a.; Ca n.a.; Al 995110; K n.a.; Mg n.a.; Na n.a.; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 60.4%. Share of metals in waste not oxidised and bulk-recyclable (exclude very small or thin parts) Iron: 0%; Alu: 100%; Copper: 0%. One kg of this waste produces 0.8342 kg of slag and 0 kg of residues, which are landfilled. Net energy production: 0MJ/kg electric energy and 0MJ/kg thermal energy. Recovery of metal scrap to recycling: 0g iron scrap, 308.48g aluminium scrap, 0g copper scrap.; Formula: Al;; UUID: 5c102778-f159-403b-ae4f-587d7690ac4f
Waste incineration from waste reception gate further downstream (excluding transport to the MSWI plant). Waste-specific air and water emisions from incineration, auxiliary material consumption for flue gas cleaning. Short-term emissions to river water and long-term emisisons to ground water from slag compartment (from bottom ash) and residual material landfill (from solidified fly ashes and scrubber slugde). Waste-specific process energy demands for MSWI and net energy generation.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in Switzerland in 2010. Well applicable to modern incineration practices in Europe, North America or Japan.
Technology: average Swiss MSWI plants in 2010 (grate incinerators) with electrostatic precipitator for fly ash (ESP), wet flue gas scrubber and 25%  SNCR , 42.77%  SCR-high dust , 32.68%  SCR-low dust -DeNOx facilities and 0% without Denox  (weighted according to mass of burnt waste, representing Swiss average). Efficiency of iron scrap separation from slag : 58%. Efficiency of non-ferrous scrap separation from slag : 31%. Gross electric efficiency technology mix 15.84% and Gross thermal efficiency technology mix 28.51%
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference, theoretical data or other source. Transfer coefficients for modern MSWI.
Production volume: na
Sampling: fully waste-specific calculation based on literature data for average MSWI operation performance 
Extrapolations: Typical elemental transfer coefficients from current studies for modern MSWI, completed with data from coal power plants and estimates, adapted for inert/burnable waste.
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5c102778-f159-403b-ae4f-587d7690ac4f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
